---
description: Omit braces on return-only if statements in C#
globs: "**/*.cs"
alwaysApply: false
---

# Return-Only If Statements

Do not use curly braces when an `if` body is only a `return` (or only `continue` / `break` / `throw` of a single statement).

```csharp
// BAD
if (session.State != SessionState.InPlay)
{
    return;
}

// GOOD
if (session.State != SessionState.InPlay)
    return;
```

```csharp
// BAD
if (player?.Cell == null)
{
    return;
}

// GOOD
if (player?.Cell == null)
    return;
```

Keep braces when the body has more than one statement, or when the single statement is not a bare control-flow exit.
